Subject: Keep capabilities for node and name IDs held as integers in ext/dom
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Fil-C drops a pointer's capability when it is converted to an integer, so code
that later turns that integer back into a pointer traps on the access.

Lexbor gives tag, attribute, namespace and prefix names IDs that are small
integers for its built-in names and the address of the name's data otherwise,
and casts IDs above the built-in range back to pointers on lookup.
Dom\HTMLDocument trapped reading parsed element and attribute names. Convert
every such address through a weak exact pointer table, which keeps the numeric
value (so comparisons against the built-in range still hold) and recovers the
capability on lookup.

The C14N and schema-validation namespace fixups key a HashTable by node
address and turn the keys back into nodes; register those nodes the same way.

--- a/ext/dom/lexbor/lexbor/core/hash.c
+++ b/ext/dom/lexbor/lexbor/core/hash.c
@@ -10,6 +10,31 @@
 
 #include "lexbor/core/str.h"
 
+#ifdef __FILC__
+#include <stdfil.h>
+
+/* Weak: the hash tables and static data keep the entries alive. */
+static zexact_ptrtable *lexbor_hash_entry_ids;
+
+__attribute__((constructor)) static void
+lexbor_hash_entry_ids_init(void)
+{
+    lexbor_hash_entry_ids = zexact_ptrtable_new_weak();
+}
+
+uintptr_t
+lexbor_hash_entry_id(const void *entry)
+{
+    return zexact_ptrtable_encode(lexbor_hash_entry_ids, (void *) entry);
+}
+
+void *
+lexbor_hash_entry_by_id(uintptr_t id)
+{
+    return zexact_ptrtable_decode(lexbor_hash_entry_ids, id);
+}
+#endif
+
 #ifndef LEXBOR_DISABLE_INTERNAL_EXTERN
     LXB_EXTERN const lxb_char_t lexbor_str_res_map_lowercase[256];
     LXB_EXTERN const lxb_char_t lexbor_str_res_map_uppercase[256];
